[Title: -Tips-
Dandelions are actually made of 100 to 200 small flowers gathered together to look like one. Also, the difference between Western and Japanese dandelions lies in the shape of the involucre at the base of the flower. In Western dandelions, the outer involucre curls downward, while in Japanese dandelions, it points upward and inward.]

